            "confidence": 10,
            "fixability": 10,
            "explanation": {
              "text": "The `PartiallyUpdateEmployeeForCompanyAsync` method in `Presentation/Controllers/EmployeesController.cs` at line 68 is directly exposed via an HTTP PATCH endpoint (`/api/companies/{companyId}/employees/{id}`). The provided code snippet and OpenAPI specification confirm the absence of any authentication or authorization attributes (e.g., `[Authorize]`). This means the endpoint is publicly accessible without requiring any form of user authentication. An attacker can send PATCH requests to this endpoint, controlling `companyId`, `id` (via path parameters), and `patchDoc` (via request body). By guessing or iterating GUIDs, an attacker can modify employee data for any company and employee, leading to unauthorized data modification, data integrity issues, and potential privacy breaches. The existing `ModelState` validation only checks the validity of the patched model, not the authorization of the request."
